er after investor demand fell short. A second utility offering was also cut back in size in Q3. Together these show weak market appetite.\n- **Pellham is cutting its plans to match.** It will cut 2027 transformer orders by about 40%. It will resize its Q1 2027 transformer tender, which was about C$900M. It will also defer two substation programmes \"until financing improves\", so equity is now the binding constraint.\n- **The other plans carry the same risk.** Pellham had planned 2027 spending up 18%. Norvane Utilities plans spending up 12%, with a C$450M tender in Q2. If Norvane needs new equity, it faces the same weak demand. I found nothing on whether it does.\n- **Implication for equity-funded spending.** Plans that depend on equity will likely be scaled back or delayed, as Pellham's are. Plans funded by debt or internal cash are less exposed. The debt side is covered separately by n3 and n5.\n\nFor VLTX, which won 60% of the last tender round, the risk is that Pellham's order cuts and the resized Q1 tender reduce its 2027 orders.\n\nI did not pull the `utility_spreads` series or any share-price or valuation data, so this rests on the offering and tender documents alone. Sources: `pellham-offering`, `pellham-statement`, `utility-tenders`, `utility-capex-2027`.","ttft_ms":3877,"type":"result","duration_ms":33657,"uuid":"f498186f-de8d-44ab-8d76-e0664619fc7c","ttft_stream_ms":3379,"time_to_request_ms":57,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":4,"system_prompt":4,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":11,"input_hooks":1,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":2,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":5,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":0,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":6,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":3,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":2,"request_build":4},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":7,"time_to_